ouse.\" [3074] Hearing the mention of the Chimney House, the young man showed a slight surprise. [3075] \"Oh!\" he said uncertainly. \"I'll go and see.\" [3076] \"Tell him it's urgent,\" Anthony said. [3077] \"Do you have a letter of recommendation from the Earl of Carrington?\" the young man asked. [3078] \"I do have something like that,\" Anthony said. \"But I need to see Mr. Issakov immediately.\" [3079] Two minutes later, Anthony was led into a luxurious inner room, which was impressively furnished with large leather armchairs. [3080] Mr. Issakov rose to greet him. [3081] \"I hope you'll forgive this impromptu visit,\" Anthony said. \"I know you're busy, so I won't take up too much of your valuable time. I just have a business matter to discuss with you.\" [3082] Mr. Issakovitch fixed him with his bright black eyes. [3083] \"Have a smoke,\" he said abruptly, pulling out an open cigar box. [3084] \"Thank you,\" Anthony said. \"Please give me one.\" [3085] He took one out himself. [3086] \"This deal is related to Hesslegrave.\" Anthony said as he took the match, noticing Azerbaijan's determined eyes brightening up. [3087] \"The murder of Michael Prince must have ruined the whole plan.\" [3088] Mr. Azerbaijan raised his eyebrows and whispered, \"What?\" with a questioning look towards the ceiling. [3089] \"Oil.\" Anthony thoughtfully looked at the smooth table, \"Oil, what an amazing thing!\" [3090] He felt the financier slightly startled. [3091] \"Well, let's get straight to the point, shall we?\" [3092] \"Of course, Eisakstan, if those oil rights go to another company, I'm sure you wouldn't be pleased?\" [3093] \"What do you suggest?\" The other man looked him straight in the eye. [3094] \"Find a suitable heir to the throne, someone who is pro-English in attitude.\" [3095] \"Where do you suggest we find one?\" [3096] \"That's my business.\" [3097] Mr. Issaquena smiled slightly in agreement, his eyes becoming more stern and piercing. [3098] \"Is it genuine? I won't tolerate any jokes about this, do you understand?\" [3099] \"Absolutely genuine.\" [3100] \"Cash deal?\" [3101] \"Cash deal.\" [3102] \"Done deal.\" [3103] \"I don't seem to need to say much to convince you?\" Anthony curiously looked at him. [3104] Herman Isaacstan smiled. [3105] \"If I couldn't tell the truth from a lie, I wouldn't be in the position I am today.\" He said briefly, \"What are your terms?\" [3106] \"The same loan, the same terms, as you offered to Prince Michael.\" [3107] \"And yourself?\" [3108] \"For now, nothing. Just that you come to the Chimney Villa tonight.\" [3109] \"No,\" Essenstatten refused firmly, \"This is a definite no.\" [3110] \"Why?\" [3111] \"I have an important dinner engagement.\" [3112] \"Still, it would be best if you canceled that dinner. It would be better for you.\" [3113] \"What do you mean?\" [3114] Anthony looked at him for a full minute, then slowly said:\n[3115] \"Do you know that the gun has been found? The gun that killed Prince Michael. Do you know where it was found? In your suitcase.\" [3116] \"What?\" Isakov nearly jumped out of his chair, his face contorted with anger as he asked:\n[3117] \"What are you talking about? What does that mean?\" [3118] \"Let me explain.\" [3119] Anthony recounted the discovery of the gun to Isakov, who turned pale and looked terrified. [3120] \"It's all a lie.\" Isakov exclaimed after Anthony finished speaking. [3121] \"Don't get upset,\" Anthony soothed him, \"if that's the case, it's easy for you to prove your innocence.\" [3122] \"How?\" asked Isakov, perplexed. [3123] \"If I were you,\" said Anthony calmly, \"I'd go to the chimney house tonight.\" [3124] Isakov hesitated, looking at him uncertainly. [3125]\n[3126] \"You suggest I do that?\" [3127] Anthony leaned in close to Isaacstan's ear and whispered a few words. The financial expert was stunned, staring at him in disbelief. [3128] \"Are you really going to\u2026\"\n[3129] \"You'll see,\" Anthony said. [3130] Chapter Twenty-seven, October Thirteen (Continued)\n[3131] The clock in the council chamber struck nine. [3132] \"Ah,\" the Earl of Carrington sighed deeply, \"they're back, like sheep, wagging their tails one after the other, all back.\" [3133] He looked sadly around the room. [3134] \"A street singer with a monkey,\" he muttered, staring at the baron, \"and a busybody from Shiregrove Street\u2026\"\n[3135] \"That's not very friendly to say about the baron,\" Bunder protested after hearing his complaints. \"He told me you were the perfect embodiment of the British aristocracy's hospitality.\" [3136] \"I think,\u201d said the Earl of Chatham, \"he says that to everyone, without getting tired. But I'm no longer the hospitable British gentleman I used to be. Once I sell the chimney house to an American entrepreneur, I'll move to a hotel. There, if someone bothers you, you can settle the bill and leave right away.\" [3137] \"Cheer up,\u201d said Bunder, \"we may never see Mr. Fischer again.\" [3138] \"I always found him an interesting person,\u201d said the Earl of Chatham, his mood fluctuating, \"it's all your fault, you young people, for making me get involved in these things. Why did they have to hold their board meeting in my house? Why couldn't they go to Rousham, Hume Castle, or find a good villa in Stretton to hold their meeting?\" [3139] \"The atmosphere isn't right there,\u201d said Bunder.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 3:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:45:22 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[3265] \"I think the baron can reveal the truth to us.\" Anthony said. [3266] \"Me?\" the baron looked at him and then at the motionless corpse on the ground. [3267] \"Take a closer look,\" Anthony said, \"don't be fooled by the makeup. Remember, she was an actress.\" [3268] The baron looked at her again, and suddenly he became extremely surprised. [3269] \"My God,\" he took a deep breath