urned red, his eyes bulging, showing the early symptoms of a stroke. Then, he heard George whisper in a hoarse voice:\n[3285] \"Of course... of course... in any case... there's no need... the situation is too complicated... we have to be very careful.\" [3286] \"Ah!\" Lemont slammed the table, \"I don't care about all this, and the murder of Michael Prince has nothing to do with me. I only want Victor King.\" [3287] Anthony gently shook his head. [3288] \"Mr. Lemont, I'm sorry. You're very capable, but you still made a mistake. I'm about to reveal my trump card.\" [3289] He crossed the room and rang the bell, and Trudwell entered in response. [3290] \"Trudwell, there's a gentleman who came with me tonight.\" [3291] \"Yes, sir, the foreigner.\" [3292] \"Correct. Could you ask him to come here quickly?\" [3293] \"Yes, sir.\" [3294] Traddles withdrew. [3295] \"My ace, the mysterious X Mr. has arrived,\" Anthony announced. \"Can anyone guess who he is?\" [3296] \"Based on your mysterious hints this morning and your attitude this afternoon,\" Hermann Issacharoff said, \"I believe the answer is obvious. You must have used some method to find Prince Nikolai of Hesse-Slavonia.\" [3297] \"Baron, do you agree?\" [3298] \"Yes, unless you have nominated another impostor, but I do not believe so. In my opinion, your actions are above reproach.\" [3299] \"Thank you, Baron, I will not forget these words. So, everyone agrees?\" [3300] He looked around at the crowd waiting for the show to begin. Only Levin remained unresponsive, his eyes fixed intently on the table. [3301] Anthony's sharp ears caught the sound of footsteps in the hallway outside. \"But,\" he grinned, \"you're all wrong!\" [3302] He quickly walked to the door and opened it. [3303] A man stood at the door, with neatly trimmed black beard, wearing glasses, and with a dandyish air, except for the bandage wrapped around his neck. [3304] \"Allow me to introduce the real L\u00e9mon, the French secret agent.\" [3305] There was a commotion, and then Hiram Fisk's calm and reassuring voice came from the window:\n[3306] \"No escape, boy. I've been here all night, waiting for you to try. My gun is aimed at you. I'm here to arrest you. You're a smart one, aren't you?\" [3307] Chapter Twenty-Nine: Further Explanation\n[3308] \"Mr. Kidd, I think you should explain the situation to us,\" Hermann Eisenczweig said one evening. [3309] \"There's not much to explain,\" Anthony said modestly. \"I went to Dover, and Mr. Fix thought I was the King of Viktor, so he followed me. There, we found a mysterious man who had been imprisoned, and after hearing his story, we understood what was going on. It's the same old trick, where the real thing is kidnapped, and a fake is put in its place, but this time, the King of Viktor himself is involved. It seems that Inspector Bartlett has suspected his French counterpart of some shady dealings and has sent a telegram to the French authorities requesting his fingerprints and other identification.\" [3310] \"Ah!\" exclaimed the baron, \"fingerprints! And the scoundrel also mentioned the Beddington body-measuring table, didn't he?\" [3311] \"He's quite the clever one, isn't he?\" Anthony said. \"I had to give him some encouragement to fan the flames, and that way, I could confuse Lemont as much as possible. Whenever I mentioned 'the row of things' and the hiding place of the jewels, he eagerly relayed the information to his accomplices. On the other hand, he kept us all in the room. The note was for Miss White. He sent Tredwell to deliver it immediately, and Tredwell did just that, sending it to the classroom upstairs. While Lemont accused me of being King Viktor to distract us, nobody would leave the room. By the time everything was explained, the gem was already gone.\" [3312] George cleared his throat. [3313] \"Mr. Kidd, I must tell you, your actions in this matter are to be condemned,\" he said pompously. \"If there had been even the slightest flaw in your plan, we would have lost a national treasure and had no hope of recovering it. Mr. Kidd, you were extremely reckless and inexcusable.\" [3314] \"Mr. R\u00f6mer, I don't think you understand this idea yet,\" Fuchs said, drawing out his words. \"The historical artifact was not hidden behind the books in the library.\" [3315] \"Not there?\" [3316] \"Absolutely not.\" [3317] \"Actually,\" Anthony explained, \"Stapleton's little trinket represents its true meaning: the rose. On Monday afternoon, I thought of this and immediately went to the rose garden. Mr. Fitch and I thought of the same thing. Facing the sundial, walking seven steps forward, then eight steps to the left, and three steps to the right, you would arrive at the red rose bush, whose name is Richmond. The entire villa has been searched, but no one thought to look in the garden. We can organize a small excavation team tomorrow morning.\" [3318] \"So, the story about the book in the library\u2026\"\n[3319] \"It was a fabrication to lure Miss White into a trap. Mr. Fitch was watching from the balcony, waiting for the right moment to blow a whistle. I can tell you that I and Mr. Fitch set up a military cordon in the house in Dover to prevent the Red Hand from contacting the imposter Lemmon. He gave the order for them to leave, and they reported that they had done so. This made him happy to proceed with his plan and openly accuse me.\" [3320] \"Well, well,\" said the Earl of Carringham, \"Now everything is clarified, and we have a satisfactory result.\" [3321] \"There's one more thing,\" said the Duke of Austria. [3322] \"What is it?\" [3323] The financier looked steadily at Anthony. [3324] \"Why do you insist on bringing me here? Just to be a spectator and warm up the scene?\" [3325] Anthony shook his head. [3326] \"No, Mr. Esakistan. You're a busy man, your time is money. What brought you here?\" [3327] \"To discuss a loan.\" [3328] \"With whom?\" [3329] \"Prince Michael of Hesse.\" [3330] \"Exactly. Prince Michael is