3346] \"It's incredible,\" George murmured. \"I've never heard of anything so incredible. Baron, do you really believe...\"\n[3347] \"Dear Romax,\" Anthony said sternly. \"I do not intend to request support from the British Foreign Office until I have presented a compelling written argument. I suggest we adjourn now, and I will discuss the loan agreement conditions with the Baron and Mr. Issakov.\" [3348] The Baron stood up, bringing his feet together. [3349] \"To meet the King of Hesse, it is the most glorious moment of my life,\" he said solemnly. [3350] \"By the way, Baron,\" Anthony said, hooking his arm around the other man's, \"I forgot to tell you, there's an important piece of information. I'm already married.\" [3351] The Baron took a step back, his face full of disappointment. [3352] \"I knew there would be trouble,\" he said under his breath, \"Oh my God! He married a black man in Africa!\" [3353] \"Well, it's not as bad as that,\" Anthony laughed. \"She's quite white, from head to toe.\" [3354] \"Well, that's a decent match between a noble and a commoner.\" [3355] \"No, that's not it. She's going to be my queen. Don't shake your head, she's more than capable. She's a British noblewoman, her family can be traced back to King William I. Royal marriages between nobility are quite popular these days, and she knows a thing or two about Heslovakia.\" [3356]\"Oh, my!\" George Roxburgh exclaimed, breaking his usual eloquent speech. \"Could it be... could it be... Virginia Rufe?\" [3357]\"Yes,\" Anthony said. \"Virginia Rufe.\" [3358]\"Goodness, sir!\" the Earl of Carmarthen exclaimed. \"I mean... congratulations! She's a beauty.\" [3359]\"Thank you,\" Anthony said. \"She's more than that.\" [3360]However, Mr. Essex was curiously examining him. [3361] \"Excuse me, sir, when did you get married?\" [3362] Anthony smiled at him. [3363] \"Actually,\" he said, \"we got married this morning.\" [3364] Chapter 30: Anthony Takes Up New Position\n[3365] \"You all go ahead,