therhood of all under heaven, but it's not the time yet. For example, in another 10,000 years. We need patience, evolution is a slow process.\" [3376] \"Your ideas fascinate me, sir.\" Bardell's eyes sparkled. \"You would make a wise king, and I hope I'm not offending you by saying so.\" [3377] \"Thank you, Chief Bardell,\" Anthony sighed. [3378] \"You don't seem happy.\" [3379] \"I don't know, maybe it will be interesting. But fixed work is always boring, I always avoid it.\" [3380] \"But you think it's your duty, right?\" [3381] \"Oh, no! Too fanciful. It's for a woman, I can't get away from women. I would do anything for her, even become a king.\" [3382] \"That's good.\" [3383] \"I've arranged everything so that both the baron and Azerbaijan won't object. They both need a king and oil, and I... Chief Inspector Battel, have you ever felt love?\" [3384] \"I love my wife very much.\" [3385] \"Love your wife... Oh, you didn't understand what I meant. I'm not talking about that.\" [3386] \"Sorry. Your servant is waiting for you outside the window.\" [3387] \"Poussin? Ah, it is him. He's a remarkable man, fortunately, the gun went off during the fight and killed the lady. Otherwise, he would have strangled her. Then, he would have been hanged by you. He is very loyal to the House of Paulovitch, and it's strange that he followed me when Michael died, not knowing my true identity at the time.\" [3388] \"Instinct,\" said Bartel. \"Dog-like instinct.\" [3389] \"His instinct was very embarrassing to me at the time, and I was afraid I would give myself away in front of you. I'll go see what he's up to.\" [3390] He walked out through the French doors, and Bartel the chief of police stood there for a moment, watching his back. Then, he said to the panel on the wall, \"He'll make a good king.\" [3391] Outside the window, Berceuse was explaining his purpose. [3392] \"Master,\" he said, and led the way down the corridor. [3393] Anthony followed behind him, not knowing what lay ahead. [3394] After a while, Berceuse stopped and pointed forward. [3395] In the moonlight, two people were sitting on the stone bench in front. [3396] \"He's still a dog,\" Anthony thinks to himself, \"and a pointer!\" [3397] He strides over, while Boris disappears into the darkness.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 4:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:45:22 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nThey showed it to me once, but I can't remember exactly. Bunder came, and she should know.\" [2689] Bunder was walking briskly across the platform. [2690] \"I'm going to London in the Panhard after lunch,\" she said. \"Anyone want to come along? Mr. Kidd, are you going? You'll be back in time for dinner.\" [2691] \"No, thank you,\" Anthony said. \"I'm fine here and have things to do.\" [2692] \"He's afraid of me,\" Brenda said. \"Either my driving or my deadly charm. Which one do you fear, Anthony?\" [2693] \"The latter,\" Anthony said. \"Always.\" [2694] \"Brenda, dear,\" Virginia said, \"is there a secret passage to the great hall?\" [2695] \"Of course there is, but it's all moldy. It used to go from the chimney villa to Weimar Abbey. That was a long time ago, and it's all blocked now, but you can still walk about a hundred yards from one end to the other. The passage under the White Gallery is much more interesting, and so is the priest's room.\" [2696] \"We're not interested in the aesthetics of the places,\" Virginia explained. \"We have a matter of business. How do we get into the secret passage to the council chamber?\" [2697] \"There's a hinged panel that I'll show you after lunch.\" [2698] \"Thank you,\" Chief Constable Bates said. \"Can we come at 2:30?\" [2699] Bender raised an eyebrow and looked at him. [2700] \"Is it about a thief?\" she asked. [2701] At that moment, Tredwell appeared on the platform and announced:\n[2702] \"Miss, it's time for lunch.\" [2703] Chapter 23: The Rose Garden Encounter\n[2704] At 2:30, Bunder, Virginia, Chief Bardell, Mr. Lemon, and Anthony Kade gathered in the council chamber. [2705] \"Waiting for Mr. Roxemus is pointless,\" Chief Bardell said. \"This matter should be dealt with promptly.\" [2706] \"If you think someone came in through this path to kill Prince Michael, you're mistaken,\" Bandler said. \"It's impossible because the other end is completely blocked.\" [2707] \"It's not that, Duchess,\" Lemont quickly said. \"We're looking for other clues.\" [2708] \"You're looking for something, aren't you?\" Bandler immediately asked. \"Is it that infamous something?\" [2709] Lemont looked puzzled. [2710] \"Explain yourself, Bandler,\" Virginia encouraged. \"Try to clarify.\" [2711] \"That thing,\" Bunder said, \"is the Prince's historical diamond, which was stolen when I was still a child.\" [2712] \"Who told you, Miss Elinor?\" Batter asked. [2713] \"I've always known. When I was twelve, one of the servants told me.\" [2714] \"A servant,\" Batter said. \"My goodness! I should let Mr. Romax hear this.\" [2715] \"Is this a secret George has kept?\" Bunder asked. \"It's incredible! I never thought it was true. George is stupid; he must have known the servants know everything.\" [2716] She walked up to the front of the Holbein portrait and pressed a spring hidden beside it. Instantly, a panel creaked open, revealing a dark passage. [2717] \"Ladies and gentlemen, please enter,\" said Bartholomew, imitating a French play. \"Forward, dear friends, forward, forward. This is the best play of the season, and it's only sixpence.\" [2718] Lemmon and Bartholomew led the way with flashlights, followed by the others. [2719] \"The air is good and fresh here,\" said Bartholomew. \"There must be ventilation somewhere.\" [2720] He led the way. The floor was uneven, with large stones, but the walls were brick. Bunder was right; the passage was only a hundred yards long before it was blocked by fallen bricks and mortar. Barth