zed, \"don't worry, Constable. If it comes down to it, you can still arrest me. At the end of the day, you still have my footprints with a criminal history.\" [2801] However, Barton didn't laugh. [2802] \"Do you have any enemies, Mr. Kidd?\" he asked. [2803] \"The third servant at the restaurant doesn't like me,\" Anthony said casually. \"He always seems to find ways not to give me the best vegetables. Why do you ask?\" [2804] \"I've been receiving anonymous letters,\" said Sheriff Barton. \"Specifically, I received one anonymous letter.\" [2805] \"About me?\" [2806] Chief Batter did not speak, but took out a crumpled cheap piece of paper from his pocket and handed it to Anthony. It was hastily written with spelling mistakes:\n[2807]Tip [Anti] Mr. Kidd, he's not what he sees\n[2808] Anthony chuckled softly and handed the paper back to him. [2809] \"Is that it? Don't be disheartened. I'm actually a king in disguise.\" [2810] He whistled as he walked into the villa. However, when he entered the room and closed the door, his face turned solemn and stern. He sat on the edge of the bed, staring glumly at the door. [2811] \"Things are getting worse,\" Anthony thought. \"I need to do something. This is terrible...\"\n[2812] He sat there for a moment, then slowly made his way to the window, aimlessly gazing outside. After a while, his eyes fell on a spot, and his expression brightened. [2813] \"That's it,\" he said. \"The rose garden! The rose garden.\" [2814] He hurried downstairs, exiting through a side door and walking out into the garden. He made his way around to the rose garden, which had doors on both sides. He entered from the far side and headed towards the sundial, which stood in the center of the garden on a small hill. [2815] As Anthony arrived, he suddenly stopped. Another guest was already there, and both of them stared at each other in surprise. [2816] \"Mr. Fisk, I didn't expect you to be interested in roses,\" Anthony said politely. [2817] \"Sir,\" said Mr.