macy in all situations. I didn't outright reject poor Michael, but he was still hurt and gave up. Why are you so interested in Michael?\" [1498] \"Just trying to learn more, if you don't mind. You didn't see the victim, did you?\" [1499] \"No, he arrived and went straight to his room to rest.\" [1500] \"So you didn't see the body?\" [1501] Virginia looked at him curiously and shook her head. [1502] \"Do you think you could possibly take a look?\" [1503] \"With the influence of a high-ranking person, such as the Earl of Carrington, I think it should be possible. Why? Is this an order?\" [1504] \"My goodness, no,\" Anthony said, surprised. \"Would I be so presumptuous? It's just that Count Stanislaus could be Prince Michael of Hesse-Darmstadt.\" [1505] Virginia's eyes widened. [1506] \"I see,\" her face suddenly lit up with a charming smile. \"You don't think Michael hid in the room because he didn't want to see me, do you?\" [1507] \"Something like that,\" Anthony admitted. \"Someone wanted to stop you from coming to the Smoke House, and if I'm not mistaken, it's because you know about Hesse-Lobenstein.\" [1508] \"You mean the victim was an imposter?\" Virginia exclaimed suddenly. [1509] \"It's just a possibility I thought of. If you can get the Earl of Carringham to take you to see the body, we'll be able to figure it out right away.\" [1510] \"The time of death was 11:45,\" Virginia mused. \"Just when the note mentioned, it's all too extraordinary.\" [1511] \"You mean that window over there?\" Virginia asked, pointing to the window above the meeting room. \"The second one from that side?\" [1512] \"No, my room is on the other side, over by Elizabeth's side hall. What's going on?\" [1513] \"Last night, I thought I heard gunshots and went back, and the lights in that room turned on.\" [1514] \"That's strange! I don't know who's staying there, but I can ask Bunder. They might have heard the gunshots too.\" [1515] \"If so, they haven't said anything about it today. I heard from Inspector Bartlett that no one in the house heard gunshots. That's my only lead, not very reliable, but I'm still going to pursue it.\" [1516] \"It's really strange,\" Virginia pondered. [1517] They walked to the boathouse by the lake, leaning against the wall and talking. [1518] \"Let's go over everything now,\" Anthony said, \"let's take our time and row out on the lake so that the police, the American guests, and the gossiping maid can't overhear us.\" [1519] \"I heard some things from the Earl of Carringham,\" Virginia said, \"but not much. Tell me, are you Anthony Kidd or Jimmy McGregor?\" [1520] So, Anthony recounted the story he had told earlier, but with a slight difference in what he said to Virginia. From six weeks ago until he unexpectedly recognized the \"Mr. Holmes\" figure. [1521] \"By the way, Mrs. Rue,\" he said finally. \"I haven't thanked you yet for lying about me being your old friend.\" [1522] \"You are my old friend, aren't you?\" Virginia exclaimed. \"You don't think I'd have pushed the body on you and then pretend we're just acquaintances when we meet again, do you? I'm not that kind of person.\" She paused and then continued, \"You know, there's one thing that really surprises me. I had no idea that the memoir had such an unexpected mystery.\" [1523] \"You're right,\" Anthony agreed. \"There's one thing I want to ask you.\" [1524] \"What is it?\" [1525] \"When I mentioned Jimmy McGregor's name to you yesterday on Pound Street, why did you seem so surprised? Had you heard of him before?\" [1526] \"Sherlock Holmes, I have heard of him. George, my cousin George Roxborough, came to me one day and talked about a bunch of nonsense. He wanted me to come here and try to seduce this McGregor into giving up the memoir. Of course, he didn't say it like that. He talked about British ladies and all that useless stuff, but his intentions were clear. It's only poor old George who could come up with such a stupid idea. Later, I asked him a few more questions, and he started to lie to me. His lies were so bad that even a two-year-old child couldn't be fooled.\" [1527] \"Anyway, his plan seems to have succeeded,\" Anthony said. \"I came here, just as he wanted me to be Jimmy McGregor, and you were just what he wanted.\" [1528] \"But there's no memoir for poor old George! Now I have a question for you. When I said those letters weren't written by me, you said you knew. How did you know that?\" [1529] \"I do know,\" Anthony said with a smile. \"My psychological knowledge is quite solid.\" [1530] \"You mean you have confidence in my character, so...\"\n[1531] Anthony shook his head vigorously. [1532] \"Not at all. I know nothing about your character. You might have a lover and write him letters. But you wouldn't give in to blackmail. The real Virginia Ruff was terrified, but you held out.\" [1533] \"I'm curious about who the real 'Virginia Ruff' is, I mean where she is. It makes me feel like I have a doppelganger.\" [1534] Anthony lit a cigarette. [1535] \"Did you know that one of the letters was mailed from the Chimney House?\" he asked. [1536] \"What?\" Virginia was startled, \"When was the letter?\" [1537] \"There was no date on the letter, but it was quite strange.\" [1538] \"I'm sure there's no other Virginia Ruffin who has stayed at the Chimney House besides me, and if there was, the Earl of Carringham or Bunder would have told me about the coincidence of the name.\" [1539] \"Hmm, that's quite eerie. Mrs. Ruffin, I'm starting to deeply doubt the existence of the other Virginia Ruffin.\" [1540] \"She's elusive,\" Virginia agreed. [1541] \"She's hard to pin down. I think the letter-writer may have used your name intentionally.\" [1542] \"But why?\" Virginia exclaimed, \"Why would they do that?\" [1543] \"That's the very question, there's so much to investigate.\" [1544] \"Who do you think killed Michael?\" Virginia asked suddenly, \"The Red Hand Gang?\" [1545] \"Possibly,\" Anthony said, his tone conveying his displeasure, \"They have a tendency to kill innocent people.\" [1546] \"Let's get started then,\" Virginia said, \"I saw the Earl of Carrington and Lady Bander walking. Our first task is to determine if the deceased was indeed Michael.\"\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 7:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:45:22 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n\"What do you have in your hand?\" [2842] \"Just a match,\" Anthony said. [2843] Bunter studied the match thoughtfully, examining the pink matchstick and yellow matchhead. He discarded the unlit cigarette in his hand and carefully placed the match in his pocket. [2844] Chapter 24: The House at Dover\n[2845] \"If you don't mind,\" Bunter said after a couple of minutes, \"can we speed up a bit? I'm a bit behind schedule.\" [2846] Anthony thought the car's speed was already impressive, but soon realized that it was nothing compared to Bunder's version of the Panhard. [2847] \"Some people,\" as they drove through the countryside, Bunder slowed down briefly, \"won't ride in my car, like my poor old dad. He absolutely refuses to come in this old car of mine.\" [2848] Anthony secretly agreed with the Earl of Chatham's decision. Riding in Bunder's car was no joke for easily tense middle-aged people. [2849] \"But you're not tense at all,\" Bunder continued approvingly, as the car swept around a bend at half the length of its body. [2850] \"I'm trained,\" Anthony explained solemnly, \"and besides, I'm in a hurry.\" [2851] \"Should I go even faster?\" Bantam asked kindly. [2852] \"Oh, no. We're already going fifty miles an hour.\" [2853] \"I'm really curious why you're suddenly leaving,\" Bantam said, honking the horn loudly. \"But I shouldn't ask, right? Are you trying to escape the law?\" [2854] \"Maybe,\" Anthony said. \"We'll find out soon.\" [2855] \"The Scotland Yard man isn't as weak as I thought,\" Bantam mused. [2856] \"Bartle is a