n here is quite unfortunate.\" [2073] His tone almost had a threatening tone to it. [2074] \"I don't quite understand what you mean,\" Anthony said. [2075] \"Why are we being held here? The body was examined yesterday, and the prince's corpse will be transported to London tomorrow, with the cause of death listed as heart failure. Yet, no one is allowed to leave. Roxemus knows less about this than I do. He sent me to ask Constable Batter.\u201d\n[2076] \"Constable Bates has his own plans,\" Anthony said thoughtfully. \"Keeping everyone here seems to be the key to his plan.\" [2077] \"But, excuse me, Mr. Cade, you have already left,\"\n[2078] \"I'm just like a kite with a line. They've been following me the whole time, and I didn't have a chance to deal with any firearms.\" [2079] \"Ah, firearms,\" Mr. Issacson pondered. \"The weapon has not been found yet?\" [2080] \"No.\" [2081] \"Perhaps you tossed it into the lake when you passed by.\" [2082] \"Quite possible.\" [2083] \"Where's Butterfield Constable? I haven't seen him all afternoon.\" [2084] \"He went to London. I ran into him at the station.\" [2085] \"To London? Really? Did he say when he'd be back?\" [2086] \"I believe he's coming back early tomorrow morning.\" [2087] Virginia and Lord Caterham, Mr. Fitch entered together, and she gave Anthony a slight smile of welcome. [2088] \"You're back, Mr. Kidd. Did you hear about last night's excitement?\" [2089] \"Mr. Kidd, that was really,\" said Mr. Fitch, \"a thrilling night. I mistook Mrs. Rue for a robber, did you hear that?\" [2090] \"So,\" said Anthony, \"what about the real robber?\" [2091] \"He got away,\" said Mr. Fitch regretfully. [2092] \"You pour the tea,\" Lord Carterham said to Virginia. \"I don't know where Bunder went.\" [2093] Virginia performed the task and then sat down next to Anthony. [2094] \"Finish your tea and come to the boathouse with us,\" she whispered. \"Bill and I have a lot to tell you.\" [2095] Then, she joined the light-hearted conversation without a care. [2096] The boatshed meeting took place as planned. [2097] Virginia and Bill eagerly brought their news. [2098] The three agreed that the center of the lake was the only safe place for their secret meeting. As they rowed away, they recounted the events of the previous night. Bill seemed a bit downcast, he didn't like Virginia's insistence on involving this colonial family. [2099] \"That's very strange,\" Anthony said after hearing the whole story, \"what do you think?\" he asked Virginia. [2100] \"I think they're looking for something,\" she answered without hesitation, \"thieves' ideas are always ridiculous.\" [2101] \"It's clear that they think there's something in the armor. But why knock on the panel? This action seems more like looking for a secret staircase or something.\" [2102] \"I know, there's a priest's cottage at the chimney house,\" Virginia said. \"And I also think there would be a secret staircase. I can ask the Earl of Carringham. I want to know what they're looking for.\" [2103] \"It can't be the memoir,\" Anthony said. \"It's a package, definitely a small item.\" [2104] \"I think George should know,\" Virginia said. \"I don't know if I can get anything out of him, but I always feel like there's something behind all of this.\" [2105] \"You said there was only one person there,\" Anthony continued. \"But there could be another one, because you heard someone running to the door when you rushed to the window.\" [2106] \"It was so quiet,\" Virginia said. \"It might have just been my imagination.\" [2107] \"That's possible. But if it wasn't your imagination, then the second person must be someone inside the house. I'm thinking\u2026\"\n[2108] \"What are you thinking?\" Virginia asked. [2109] \"Mr. Fuchs heard someone calling for help downstairs, yet he was dressed properly.\" [2110] \"There must be more to it,\" Virginia agreed. \"And Esakistan, he's been sleeping the whole time, and that's suspicious. He couldn't have been that deep in sleep, could he?\" [2111] \"And then there's that guy Perry,\" Bill said. \"He just looks like a crook. I mean, Michael's servant.\" [2112] \"There are plenty of suspicious characters in the Chimney House,\" Virginia said. \"I'm sure the others are suspicious of us too. It would have been better if Constable Barter hadn't gone to London. He's being very unwise.\" [2113] \"It's all so puzzling,\" Anthony admitted. \"I've been wandering around outside, but I've found nothing. I've been so frustrated, I've almost cried. I think the key to this mystery is this: did they find what they were looking for last night?\" [2114] \"What if they didn't?\" Virginia asked. \"In fact, I'm sure they didn't.\" [2115] \"Then I think they'll come back. They know, or they'll soon know, that Constable Barter has gone to London. They'll take advantage of the opportunity and come back tonight.\" [2116] \"Do you really think so?\" [2117] \"It's an opportunity.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 10:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:45:22 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nHe revived Prince Nikolai, using that identity, and tricked a lot of American money out of him with the supposed oil rights. But an accidental slip exposed his identity, so he hurriedly left the country. This time, he's come to England. That's why I'm here. He'll come to the Chimney House sooner or later, if he hasn't already!\" [2230] \"You think?\" [2231] \"I believe that Prince Michael was here on the night he was killed, and he came back last night.\" [2232] \"Is it to try again?\" said Batter. [2233] \"Yes.\" [2234] \"What has been bothering me,\" Balthasar continued, \"is the mystery surrounding what happened to Monsieur Lemaire. Paris told me that he was cooperating with my work, but I don't understand why he hasn't shown up.\" [2235] \"I must apologize,\" said Lemon, \"I arrived the day after the murder, and I immediately thought that it would be possible to investigate in an unofficial capacity, instead of as a colleague. This would have greatly increased the chances of solving the case, of course, but it would have also made me a suspect, which could have been helpful for my plan, as it would have made the person I was following let their guard down. In the past two days, I have indeed seen some interesting things.\" [2236] \"But,\" said Bill, \"what happened last night?\" [2237] \"I'm afraid,\" said Mr. Lemmon, \"that I caused you a lot of trouble.\" [2238] \"I was chasing you?\" [2239] \"Yes, let me explain. Prince Michael was killed in this room, so I came here to investigate. I was standing on the platform outside and soon saw someone moving around inside, with the occasional flash of a flashlight. I tried the middle window and found it unlocked. I don't know if the person had come in through that window before or if they left it unlocked on purpose to provide an alibi. I quietly opened the window and slipped inside. I slowly made my way around, finally finding a spot where I could see the other person's movements without being seen myself. I couldn't see who it was, but I could see their silhouette against the light from the flashlight, so I could only see them vaguely. However, their actions puzzled me, as they were disassembling the two armor figures and examining each piece. When they realized there was nothing inside, they began tapping on the panel beneath the portrait. I don't know what they were going to do next, as they were interrupted by your sudden arrival\u2026\" He looked at Bill. [2240] \"We were well-intentioned but made a mess of things,\" Virginia pondered. [2241] \"Madam, that's true. He immediately turned off the flashlight. I didn't want to reveal my identity, so I jumped out of the window. I bumped into two people in the dark and fell to the ground. I immediately got up and escaped out of the window. Mr. Everleigh mistook me for the intruder and chased